## Shared chart renderers

`CHART` lowers to the same `sumUI.ChartSpec` used by Python. The native SumGUI renderer is the default; Matplotlib and Seaborn are optional ChartSpec renderers (`sumbasic[charts]`). Named CHART syntax accepts `\` or `_` line continuation.

## Text-cell mouse input

`MOUSEX()` and `MOUSEY()` return one-based text-cell coordinates matching
`LOCATE row,column`. `MOUSEBUTTON()` returns a pending left click as `1` and
consumes it, returning `0` until the next click. Clicks work in the textual
Output plane of both sumIDE backends. Interactive POSIX `--run` also enables
SGR mouse reporting when the terminal supports it.

```basic
IF MOUSEBUTTON() = 1 THEN
    PRINT MOUSEX(); ","; MOUSEY()
END IF
```

`examples/piano_text.bas` draws as many keys as fit in the current text
viewport and accepts both mouse clicks and the 29-key chromatic mapping
`zsxdcvgbhnjm`, `q2w3er5t6y7u`, `i9o0p`. Audio is produced exclusively by
the existing PLAY synthesizer. `PLAY HOLD 3, note$` sustains a note, renews its
three-second safety timeout without retriggering on keyboard repeat, and stops
immediately on graphical `KEYUP$` or mouse/touch release.

<p align=center><b>- oOo -</b></p>
